            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="KEA01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Thomas</forename>
                        <surname>Kearsley</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1773">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death notBefore="1800" notAfter="1802"/>
                    <occupation>artist</occupation>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Thomas Kearsley was a portrait painter who painted Godwin in 1794.</p>
                        <p><persName key="KEA04">George Kearsley</persName>, a bookseller who published <title>Cursory Strictures</title> also appears in the diary (his father, also George,
    published <title>Life of Chatham</title>). However, given that Thomas is the Kearsley noted in the 1796 list of notable acquaintances (Godwin
      met him in 1793), almost all the Kearsleys have been coded as Thomas. There are two instances of Kearsley which can be identified as George - one associated with
    George Robinson, prior to 1793 and one associated with <title>Cursory Strictures</title>.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="printedbook">St Clair</bibl>
